From 69b29a483d1df42745358d4dd872cee2d7334daf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lineage-build <build@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:59:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cancunf: Add AppSetup, a first-run installer and updater

Installs and updates apps that ship outside the image: sandboxed
Google Play (GmsCore and the Play Store, from GrapheneOS's signed app
index), Aurora Store, F-Droid and Titanium Browser. Keeping them out of
the image keeps the OTA under GitHub's 2 GiB limit (Titanium alone is
335 MB) and lets each update on its own schedule.

Every download must be signed by a pinned certificate before it is
installed, whatever server served it; the GrapheneOS index must carry
a valid Ed25519 signature from its pinned key and may not be older
than one already seen; downgrades are refused. It is a priv-app with
INSTALL_PACKAGES, so one tap installs everything, and a daily job on
unmetered networks updates the apps that are installed.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
